# Amazon OAuth integration examples
#
# Replace variables before running with an HTTP client that supports .http files.

@base_url = http://localhost:8000
@tenant_id = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@marketplace_id = A2VIGQ35RCS4UG

### Health
GET {{base_url}}/health

### API health
GET {{base_url}}/api/health

### Generate Seller Central authorization URL for Europe
GET {{base_url}}/api/auth/amazon/test-login?tenant_id={{tenant_id}}&region=europe&marketplace_id={{marketplace_id}}

### Generate Seller Central authorization URL for North America
GET {{base_url}}/api/auth/amazon/test-login?tenant_id={{tenant_id}}&region=north_america&marketplace_id=ATVPDKIKX0DER

### Generate Seller Central authorization URL for Far East
GET {{base_url}}/api/auth/amazon/test-login?tenant_id={{tenant_id}}&region=far_east&marketplace_id=A1VC38T7YXB528

### Amazon callback after Seller Central redirects back
GET {{base_url}}/api/auth/amazon/callback?state=<state>&spapi_oauth_code=<code>&selling_partner_id=<seller_id>&marketplace_id={{marketplace_id}}

### Check Amazon authorization status
GET {{base_url}}/api/auth/amazon/status?tenant_id={{tenant_id}}
